r term, including 3 × 50 + 1 = 151.\nThey tested pattern membership by checking whether the resulting n was a whole number.\nTeach-back was not passed; the calendar-pattern explanation remained unclear.","parentNote":"Reyansh practised describing growing patterns with algebraic rules and using those rules to find distant terms or test membership. They explained that 5n + 3 represents adding 5 each round, and they used whole-number values of n to decide whether 200 belonged to a pattern. One calendar-pattern explanation was still unclear at the end. At home, ask them to make a short pattern, write its rule, and check one number by solving for n.","did":{"title":"Patterns and relationships with algebra","shortTitle":"Algebra patterns","cards":[{"kind":"item","ask":"Teeliyan: 4, 7, 10, 13, ... 50va term kaise nikaalenge?","answer":"Use a rule like 3n + 1","tick":true,"withHelp":false,"turnSeq":22},{"kind":"item","ask":"Pattern aise hi chale, toh round n ke points ka rule likhiye.","answer":"उम्म... 5n + 3? हर राउंड में 5 जुड़ रहा है...","tick":true,"withHelp":false,"turnSeq":12},{"kind":"item","ask":"Khaali jagah bhariye: 30th term: 3 × 30 + 2 = ___.","answer":"umm... 92? 3 × 30 = 90... + 2 = 92","tick":true,"withHelp":true,"turnSeq":10}],"nextTitle":"Multiplying fractions","face":"warm","teacher":{"id":"asha","name":"Asha","characterName":"Asha","addressedAs":"Asha didi","pronouns":{"subject":"she","object":"her","possessive":"her"},"voice":"marin","role":"AI teacher","lookRev":1,"signatureColor":"#3E7C74"},"revoiceSeq":22},"facts":{"topic":"Patterns and relationships with algebra","minutes":0.9,"teachbackPassed":false,"skills":[{"skill":"Describe a growing pattern with an algebraic rule","attempts":3,"unaidedCorrect":2},{"skill":"Use a rule to find far terms and to test whether a number belongs to a pattern","attempts":3,"unaidedCorrect":2}],"misconceptions":[]}},"start":{"ms":1488,"topic":{"id":"c7-maths-ch04-t03","title":"Patterns and relationships with algebra","c